            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "My suggestion would be to use [`buf_lines` picker from 'mini.extra'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4228f166ee9db3e910eea1915e2d3683028add47/doc/mini-extra.txt#L231). You can use it like this: `:Pick buf_lines scope='current'`.\r\nIt won't use `rg` instead relying on default 'mini.pick' matching, but I'd argue `rg` is not needed here.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">My suggestion would be to use <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4228f166ee9db3e910eea1915e2d3683028add47/doc/mini-extra.txt#L231\"><code class=\"notranslate\">buf_lines</code> picker from 'mini.extra'</a>. You can use it like this: <code class=\"notranslate\">:Pick buf_lines scope='current'</code>.<br>\nIt won't use <code class=\"notranslate\">rg</code> instead relying on default 'mini.pick' matching, but I'd argue <code class=\"notranslate\">rg</code> is not needed here.</p>",
            "bodyText": "My suggestion would be to use buf_lines picker from 'mini.extra'. You can use it like this: :Pick buf_lines scope='current'.\nIt won't use rg instead relying on default 'mini.pick' matching, but I'd argue rg is not needed here.",
